/*
:name: undefined_port_width
:type: error
:error: read of undefined variable 'ZZ'
:help: declare it
*/

// Ruling 2026-09-28 #24 (clarification): reading a name with no accessible
// declaration is a direct compile error at the read. A port width bound that
// does not fold is not lowered where it is written, so nothing recorded the
// read: an undeclared `ZZ` only warned "not a compile-time value" and the
// width was SILENTLY dropped (the port compiled as the full 8-bit argument).
pub comb undefined_port_width(a:Unsigned(bits=ZZ)) -> (r:U8) {  // locate_error_here
  r = a
}
